<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Laptop-side twin for the 'Humanoid_Travel' WIFI link.  Created 2026-09-28.
     Use with the viewer:
         export CYCLONEDDS_URI=file://.../config/cyclonedds_laptop_wifi.xml

     The laptop used to reach Stuart over a cable into its own 192.168.123.x
     port, so the wired twin binds enp2s0 and Stuart saw the laptop at
     192.168.123.99.  The operator moved to the travel router instead
     ('i have connected it through Humanoid_Travel Wifi such that now i dont
     need cable to ssh in'):
         enp2s0  DOWN                       <- old cable, gone
         wlo1    UP  192.168.123.137/24     <- Humanoid_Travel
     The router hands out the SAME 192.168.123.x subnet as the old cable and
     bridges its WiFi to its ethernet ports, which is why Stuart is still
     reachable at 192.168.123.164 unchanged (verified 2026-09-28: ping over
     wlo1, ARP 3c:6d:66:16:63:90 REACHABLE, 21 ROS2 topics discovered).
     So only the INTERFACE and the LAPTOP'S OWN ADDRESS moved.

     Paired robot-side file: /home/unitree/cyclonedds_wifi.xml
     (robot stays on eth0 there; wlan0 is 192.168.0.165/24, a different
     network entirely, the robot's internet, NOT the laptop's path).

     192.168.123.137 is a DHCP lease from the travel router.  If the laptop
     is ever handed a different address, the robot's Peer goes stale and the
     viewer shows its four topics MISSING while everything else looks fine.
     Reserve it in the router if possible.

     NOTE (measured 2026-09-28): the laptop associates on 2.4 GHz channel 1
     while 'Humanoid_Travel_5G' is available at 95% signal on 5 GHz ch165.
     The 2.4 GHz band showed 6 ms - 2774 ms RTT to the router, which is enough
     loss/latency that the 305 KB /camera/color/image_raw frame does not
     survive the trip.  Prefer the 5 GHz SSID. -->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <NetworkInterfaceAddress>wlo1</NetworkInterfaceAddress>
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
      <!-- B8k (2026-10-16): Stuart now allows 31 DDS participants (index 0-30).  Without
           this the laptop only probes Stuart's ports for index 0-9, so a node that got
           index 10+ (seen: yolo_node) is invisible here: /detections had 0 publishers. -->
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>30</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
      <Peers>
        <Peer address="127.0.0.1"/>
        <Peer address="192.168.123.164"/>
      </Peers>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
